# Printing: Paramètres > Appareils > Imprimantes et scanners (shell/main/ipc/printers.js, shell/main/lib/cups.js,
# aurora-admin printer-* actions) and the print dialog (printers:print -> lp).
# Driverless only: IPP Everywhere / AirPrint / Mopria printers (nearly every network or USB printer sold since ~2015)
# are added with `lpadmin -m everywhere`; CUPS asks the printer itself for its capabilities, no PPD or vendor driver.
# Not in the image: printer-driver-gutenprint / hplip (vendor drivers for older printers, tens of MB with their Python
# and data dependencies) — they can be installed from the Store when an old printer needs them.
# Not in the image: cups-browsed (CUPS 2.4 already offers network IPP printers as temporary destinations, the add
# list in Paramètres covers the rest, and it was the entry point of the 2024 remote CUPS vulnerabilities).
# cups pulls cups-daemon, cups-client (lp, lpstat, lpadmin, cancel, cupsenable…), cups-filters, ghostscript, poppler-utils.
cups
cups-filters
# ipptool: ink / toner levels of a queue (marker-levels) for Paramètres.
cups-ipp-utils
# USB printers that speak IPP-over-USB (IPP Everywhere through USB), shared on localhost and announced over DNS-SD.
ipp-usb
# DNS-SD / mDNS: discovery of network printers (avahi-browse in Paramètres) and *.local host names (libnss-mdns).
avahi-daemon
avahi-utils
libnss-mdns
